# Infinite Queue Consumer (Directive v6)

Read `docs/QUEUE_STATE.md` → pick **current_task** → execute → update state → **immediately start next task**.

## Mode

**Release Queue Consumer.** Not Mission Mode. Not batch-complete mode.

- Never wait for "다음 작업"
- Never wait for "다음 Release"
- Never mid-report "완료"
- Consume Roadmap until last task or PM gate

## Hierarchy

```
Release → Product → Mission → Epic → Sprint → Feature → Task → Sub-task
```

Task done ≠ Mission done. Mission done ≠ Release done. Release done ≠ project done.

## Cycle (per Task, no approval)

Implement → QA → Commit → Push → Production → Tag → Release Note → ROADMAP update → **next Task auto-start**

No PM approval · No CPO approval · No questions.

## Stop only when

1. Roadmap last task complete
2. PM gate: LLM · DB · Billing · Auth · external cost
3. Build failure (fix and resume)
4. Production outage (fix and resume)
5. CPO direct stop order

## Forbidden output

다음 작업은… · 승인해 주세요 · 배포할까요 · 진행할까요 · Release N 완료 · Mission N 완료

## Reporting

**08:00 KST Daily Production Report only** — template: `docs/templates/DAILY_AUTONOMOUS_REPORT.md`

## Task quality (every Task)

UX · Animation · Responsive · A11y · Analytics · Admin · Error · Loading · Empty · Offline · Retry · SEO · Perf · Telemetry · History · Docs · Tests · Release note

## Product north star

Not a feature factory — **AI Strategy PM**: user thinks less, project progresses itself.

